## 1. Definitions

- **"Software"** — the source code, documentation, configuration, stylesheets,
  scripts, icons and other materials in this repository, excluding the
  Third-Party Materials described in Section 8.
- **"Licensor"** — Mensura Media, the copyright holder.
- **"You"** — the individual exercising the permissions in this Licence.
- **"Personal Use"** — use by a natural person for their own private study,
  learning, evaluation or curiosity, and for no other purpose.
- **"Commercial Use"** — any use intended for or directed toward commercial
  advantage or monetary compensation, including without limitation: use within
  a business, institution or organisation; use in providing a paid or ad-funded
  service; bundling with a product offered for sale; use in paid tuition,
  training or coursework delivery; and internal use by any entity in the course
  of its operations.
- **"Curated Data"** — the character sets, readings, meanings, thematic
  categories, visual-confusion pair list, frequency ordering and other compiled
  data in `src/japanese_practice/content/`, together with the selection,
  arrangement and correction of that data. Individual Japanese characters are
  not owned by anyone; the compilation is.
- **"Derivative Application"** — any software that is a flash-card,
  spaced-repetition, character-drill, vocabulary or other language-learning
  application, and that is created wholly or partly by copying, adapting,
  translating, porting, reimplementing or otherwise deriving from the Software
  or the Curated Data. Rewriting the Software in another programming language,
  framework or runtime does not stop the result being a Derivative Application.
- **"Attribution Notice"** — the notice specified in Section 5.2.

